# Tailwind & Styling Standards

## Utility-First

- Use Tailwind utility classes directly, not custom CSS (except global resets)
- Use `cn()` helper for conditional classes:

```tsx
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

<div className={cn("rounded-lg border p-4", isOverdue && "border-red-500 bg-red-50")} />
```

## Design Tokens

Use shadcn/ui CSS variables, not hardcoded colors:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded colors
<p className="text-gray-500 bg-white border-gray-200">

// ✅ GOOD — semantic tokens (adapt to theming)
<p className="text-muted-foreground bg-background border-border">
```

## Responsive Design

Mobile-first. Always start with the smallest screen and layer up:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — desktop-first
<div className="grid grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-1">

// ✅ GOOD — mobile-first
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
```

Breakpoints: `sm` (640px) · `md` (768px) · `lg` (1024px) · `xl` (1280px)

## Component Patterns

- Status badges: use consistent color mapping across the app

```tsx
const STATUS_COLORS: Record<AssignmentStatus, string> = {
  draft: "bg-gray-100 text-gray-700",
  assigned: "bg-blue-100 text-blue-700",
  in_progress: "bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700",
  under_review: "bg-purple-100 text-purple-700",
  completed: "bg-green-100 text-green-700",
  closed: "bg-gray-200 text-gray-500",
};
```

- Spacing: prefer `p-4`, `gap-4`, `space-y-4` (multiples of 4) for consistency
- Never use inline `style={}` unless dynamically calculated (e.g., chart widths)

## Accessibility

- Interactive elements must have `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring`
- Use semantic HTML (`<button>` not `<div onClick>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`)
- All images need `alt` text; decorative images get `alt=""`
- Form inputs must have associated `<label>` elements
